    <forecast>
        <area aac="SA_FA001" description="South Australia" type="region">
            <forecast-period start-time-local="2026-11-25T09:20:28+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-25T09:20:28+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-11-24T22:50:28Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-24T22:50:28Z">
                <text type="warning_summary_footer">For latest warnings go to www.bom.gov.au, subscribe to RSS feeds, call 1300 659 210* or listen for warnings on relevant TV and radio broadcasts.</text>
                <text type="synoptic_situation">A trough of low pressure over the far northeast will linger near the far northeast until mid week. A high pressure to the east extends a ridge across southern SA. A trough of low pressure approaches the western border today then moves across the west and north of the State on Thursday and eastern parts on Friday. Another ridge pushes into the west later Friday and over the weekend.</text>
                <text type="product_footer">* Calls to 1300 numbers cost around 27.5c incl. GST, higher from mobiles or public phones.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
        <area aac="SA_PW011" description="Eastern Eyre Peninsula" type="public-district" parent-aac="SA_FA001">
            <forecast-period index="0" start-time-local="2026-11-25T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-26T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-11-24T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-25T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Mostly sunny. Winds north to northwesterly 15 to 20 km/h shifting south to southeasterly 20 to 30 km/h in the early afternoon. Daytime maximum temperatures in the low to mid 30s.</text>
                <text type="fire_danger">High</text>
                <text type="uv_alert">Sun protection 9:00am to 5:10pm, UV Index predicted to reach 11 [Extreme]</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="1" start-time-local="2026-11-26T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-27T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-11-25T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-26T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Cloudy. Medium chance of showers, most likely in the evening. Winds southeast to southwesterly 15 to 25 km/h tending northeast to southeasterly in the early afternoon then tending southeast to southwesterly 15 to 20 km/h in the late evening. Overnight temperatures falling to around 16 with daytime temperatures reaching around 30.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="2" start-time-local="2026-11-27T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-28T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-11-26T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-27T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. Slight chance of a shower in the morning. Winds southeasterly 15 to 20 km/h turning south to southwesterly 20 to 30 km/h during the afternoon. Overnight temperatures falling to around 16 with daytime temperatures reaching around 30.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="3" start-time-local="2026-11-28T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-29T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-11-27T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-28T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. Slight chance of a shower in the morning and afternoon. Winds south to southwesterly 25 to 40 km/h. Overnight temperatures falling to between 12 and 15 with daytime temperatures reaching 24 to 29.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
